{"availability":"available","full":"sirrommit/chromebook-checkout","name":"chromebook-checkout","description":"Self-service checkout kiosk for school loaner Chromebooks. Static files, no backend, no student data in the repo.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-25T18:33:17Z","updated":"2026-08-25T18:43:31Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sirrommit.github.io/chromebook-checkout/","topics":["chromeos","kiosk","pwa","school-it"],"demo":"https://sirrommit.github.io/chromebook-checkout/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:48.244Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:48.244Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:48.244Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T05:44:48.244Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A self-service checkout kiosk for a small fleet of loaner Chromebooks at a school front desk. A student taps a number, types their email, and picks a return-by date. Staff can see who has what, and for how long, from a password-protected screen on the same machine.","Built for a specific situation: a shelf of loaners, one checkout point, and a front-desk staff member who shouldn't have to stop what they're doing every time a student needs one. If that's your situation too, you're welcome to it.","There is no server and no database. The whole thing is static files. Every event is appended to a CSV file in the browser's origin private file system on the kiosk, and exported with a button when you want to analyse usage in Sheets."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sirrommit/chromebook-checkout/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5fc65c0a8abe49114583404426e455a2d65e42a4a781dfecf49af55410e8c4a3","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:48.400Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:48.400Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A self-service checkout kiosk for a small fleet of loaner Chromebooks at a school front desk. A stu